      mastery_orientation: [72, 0.58, "s", "A"],
      // [src_delacroix_baudelaire, src_delacroix_csm | later career | friend + press] Baudelaire says that once he had started, he stopped only when overcome by physical fatigue, and that in later years work replaced pleasure; the Monitor calls him a man of endless industry. Both rest on the same kind of general characterisation, and Baudelaire is a close admirer. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): lowered from 70 / 0.52 because the claim rests on one admiring friend's general description and a press summary, with no dated instance of a specific absorbed work session.
      deep_focus: [64, 0.45, "i", "D"],
